WEBVTT

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.310
What should I do, Kotori?

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:12.950
I'm not so sure myself.
This is a bit unexpected.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:19.830
Well, anime and manga characters
are ideal companions, in a way.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:25.040
When you compare them to real people,
reality seems like a letdown.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.710
Speaking from experience?

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:33.170
Tsk, tsk, tsk. I fancy
voice actresses, too, Commander.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.800
Okay then.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.890
Commander. Didn't Nia say
she liked some character?

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.600
Tokiya. Girls seem to love him.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.640
I see...

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.900
Shido, help is on the way.
Just follow my plan to the word.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:55.070
He's taking forever.
Strategizing with Kotori, maybe?

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.160
Oh, there you are--

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.050
It's Tokiya.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.800
From <i>Chronicle</i>?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.260
That costume's legit!

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.470
This seat's mine, woman.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.270
Tokiya...? Why?

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:55.440
Mind yourself, woman.
I didn't say you can use my name.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.820
Back off, woman.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.450
Happiness climbing!

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.660
Sealing levels reached.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.870
It worked, Shido! Go for it!

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.000
Huh? What's wrong?

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:16.960
Shut your mouth.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.800
As if!

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.840
Eh?

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.600
Happiness falling!

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.430
It's lower than ever!

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.180
No way! Why?!

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.610
What the hell were you thinking?

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.770
Huh? Meaning?

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:41.820
Tokiya would never make moves
on a woman! Use common sense!

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.360
Common sense?

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:49.950
Tokiya's on a journey to avenge
his little sister and lover, Hibari!

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:55.460
As a lonely observer, I wouldn't dare
intrude on that beautiful world!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.590
Don't break the fourth wall!
Don't break it!

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.840
Hey! Calm down, Nia!

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.930
Tokiya would never do that!

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:08.720
If you wanna make me fall for you,
come back when you're 2D!

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.390
Well, that didn't work out.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:17.690
Oh my. You sure took a beating.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.900
And who's fault is that?!

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:25.780
Commander. The plan failed,
but it's true that her levels rose.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.280
Precisely.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:33.160
In other words, if a character
she likes is brought to life,

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.460
it's possible to raise her happiness.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:39.250
So, 2.5D will work.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.670
In that case...!

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.720
Was that a bit cruel of me?

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:55.270
I guess ditching him there
wasn't the nicest thing.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:59.150
Maybe I should've let him kiss me.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:04.440
Though, Spirit power can't be sealed
unless you open your heart.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:10.200
He seems like a good guy,
but 3D doesn't do it for me...

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:18.330
Argh! What the hell should I do?!
Just tell me, Raziel!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.550
Huh?

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.880
Hello. Delivery.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.060
"Demo"

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:37.270
"As thanks for your services,
we've sent you a demo of a new game."

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:41.940
Really? Have I done work
for this company before?

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:47.400
Looks like a school-based <i>otome</i> game.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:49.950
"Please input your name..."
"Back | OK"

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:54.410
Nia... Honjo...

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.870
"Birthday: 2/29
Nia Honjo"
"Back | OK"

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:06.170
Hey, are you the new transfer student?
I'm Shido Itsuki. Nice to meet you.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:11.090
He looks awfully like Boy...
Just a coincidence?

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.850
You're so funny, Nia.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:21.400
Whoa! He spoke my name?!
And it sounded so natural, too!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.690
Games sure have come far
in the past five years!

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:30.320
Next Saturday, huh?
Sure. Where should we go?

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.120
"Enter your date plans"

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.370
You're kidding! I can write anything?!

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:38.870
"Enter your date plans"
"I wanna buy doujinshi in Akiba"

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.870
There's no way this works.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:43.130
Doujinshi in Akiba?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.920
That's so like you. It's a date.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:54.180
This dialogue! This freedom!
Are games really this advanced?!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:58.600
Science is fricken' awesome!

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:02.100
Oh? You like these kinda books?

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:08.280
No, it's all good. I think
having passions is a wonderful thing.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.570
She's played for two hours.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:13.570
Happiness is rising steadily.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:20.580
Once Nia's done with the game,
Shido can appear before her as "Itsuki."

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.750
Seeing how it's really him,
there's nothing to screw up.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.460
Ah... Incredible!

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:34.970
But it's just a demo,
so I'll have to buy the real version.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:39.220
Has this publisher made anything else?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.140
I'll just ask Raziel.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.570
Oh, shoot!

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.610
Huh?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.860
Grr! This was all your doing?!

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.950
"Emergency Meeting"
"How to make Nia Honjo fall for Shido!?"

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:58.240
Well, now we've really pissed her off.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:04.330
"Tohka Yatogami"

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:04.580
I'm not surprised. You guys used
a fake game to basically spy on her.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:09.340
Hey, Shido. Why does Nia only like 2D?

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:19.220
"Kotori Itsuka"

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.550
Huh? Well...

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.470
I wondered that, too.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:19.600
Reine is checking if
she had any manga artist pals.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:25.150
Suggestion. Shouldn't we just
make Shido suit her preferences?

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:30.940
We're talking 2D, though.
Should we flatten him with a steamroller?

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:31.780
Eh?!

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:37.200
"Natsumi"

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:37.450
In that case, what if I made him
into a manga page with Haniel?

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:41.330
Hold your horses! Making me 2D is nuts!

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:47.000
"Origami Tobiichi"

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:45.120
I think Natsumi has the right idea.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.040
Let's put Shido on a page.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:53.260
"Emergency Meeting"
"How to make Nia Honjo fall for Shido!?"

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.250
--What?
--Huh?

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.960
Though, not by
transforming Shido himself,

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:56.760
but by making a manga
where Shido is a character.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:57.800
Wha--?!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:01.890
I see! That's a way of making him 2D!

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:07.150
"Yuzuru Yamai"

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:07.520
Mm! It'll be fine as long as
we write stuff that's true.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:16.280
"Yoshino"

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:12.900
Yeah. If Nia knows about
everything Shido's done for us,

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.530
I'm sure she'll end up liking Shido, too.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.280
Really, guys?

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:23.750
Ooh! Shido in a manga!
That's awesome! I wanna help!

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:29.420
Agreement. After tying in our 39th match,
"Best Manga Submission,"

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:34.460
the two of us are due
to put our skills back to the test.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:38.010
You guys sure compete over everything.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.930
The outside line? I wonder who it is?

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:46.100
Yo! Plotting something, are we?

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:52.690
I had Raziel tell me about this line...
and about what you're planning.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:57.150
Still, even if you do make a manga,

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.740
why do you just assume that I'll read it?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:06.500
I might've taken a look at it before,

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.080
but you guys have put me in "angry mode."

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:14.170
With Comico coming up,
I can't waste my time.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:17.720
Comico? You're entering Comico?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.220
Yup. My first in five years.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.140
Miku, what's Comico?

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.810
Comic Colosseum.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:30.690
It's a convention for people
to sell the doujinshi they make.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:36.150
If our manga was worth reading,
would you take the time to read it?

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.360
Hmm?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:44.080
For example, if our manga manages
to sell more copies than yours at Comico.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.200
Oh? You're actually serious?

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:52.790
Yeah. If we end up winning,
you have to read our manga.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.050
Okay! You're on!

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:03.550
You think you can beat
Souji Honjo, do you?

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:07.020
H-Hey, Kotori...

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:12.060
Don't worry. I've got a plan.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.570
They underestimate me.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.950
They really think they can beat a pro?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:30.330
Regardless of what happens, it's not like
I could like a real person anyway.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:36.960
Besides, it's not like
anyone would like me, either.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:43.180
That's the all-knowing Angel,
Raziel, is it not?

00:11:53.940 --> 00:12:00.650
Nice to meet you, Nia Honjo.
My name is Kurumi Tokisaki.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:17.790
Kurumi Tokisaki,
the Spirit who manipulates time...

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:22.010
I see. You're the one
who saved me from DEM.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.840
That saves an explanation.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:29.010
You're the second Spirit
seen after the "Spirit of Origin."

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:32.350
I've been longing to meet you.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:35.980
Hmm? And why's that?

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:42.070
No need to be on your guard.
I just came to ask a favor.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:47.950
Could you look into something with Raziel?

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:51.450
Tell me about the Spirit of Origin...

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.960
...and how to kill it.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.550
Whoa! This is neat!

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.260
It's so "professional."

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:09.550
Comico's in two days.
Can we do it in time?

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:14.060
We'll have to.
Let's see how well everyone draws.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:16.060
You draw something, too.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.400
Me?

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:22.860
Didn't you use to sketch all the time?

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:24.900
The Black Knight, Lievan, or something?

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:28.320
"The Black Knight, Lievan"

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.710
If you're done drawing, let's see it!

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.710
I see... Yeah, very cute.

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:42.050
Really?!

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:46.260
Yeah, but I don't think
it'll work for us this time.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.680
Oh...

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.760
S-Sorry.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:55.680
Next one! Next!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.730
No fair, Darling!

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:04.110
Whoa! You guys are pretty good!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:09.110
So far, you two are our
best candidates. So, who's next?

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.950
What did you draw, Origami?!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.500
Shido and me, becoming one.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.830
No one asked you to draw that!

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:26.130
If we're trying to sell doujinshi,
going 18+ is the way to go.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:30.340
We're entering as
a "General Audience" booth, you know.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:35.850
What's up? If you drew something,
let's see it. C'mon.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:40.520
Um, it's bad, so don't expect much.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:45.570
I didn't sleep well last night,
and I haven't drawn in forever.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.650
Okay, fine. Just show us already!

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:56.370
Incredible, Natsumi!
Who knew you had such skill?!

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:59.210
Well, I wouldn't say "skill."

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:04.170
But I did imitate
a manga artist once, just for fun.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.260
That settles it!
Natsumi's our main artist.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:11.720
With Yuzuru, Kaguya, Shido,
and Origami supporting her.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.600
Roger that!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:17.100
A-Are you really fine with me?

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:21.640
Of course! We need your talent
to help Nia, Natsumi!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:27.110
Don't complain about it later.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:30.240
Kotori, what can the rest of us do?

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:34.030
I have another job for you guys.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:37.910
In a way, it's more important
than the manga.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:38.910
Hmm?

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.050
Well then...

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.640
That's troubling news.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.060
What do you suppose we do?

00:15:57.060 --> 00:16:00.980
Indeed. According to what
Raziel had to say,

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:07.270
even if I gather Spirit power, I stand
no chance against the Spirit of Origin.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.280
But...

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.910
...what does it matter anyway?

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.870
I'm the Spirit with power over time.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:22.040
The notion of time makes
everything else insignificant.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.920
Gah! Messed up the grid.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.670
Geh! The tears are invading the white!

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:36.680
Likewise. The ink spread under the ruler.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:40.310
It's okay. This can be fixed.

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:42.980
Shido, got a minute?

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.480
I'm Hiroki Takajo.

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.360
The manga artist!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:58.200
Yes. Looking into Nia's--that is,
Souji Honjo's friends, led me to her.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:02.620
I hear you guys are relatives of Honjo's?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:08.210
Yeah. We're worried since
we're having trouble contacting Nia.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:13.050
So, we're hoping you can share
anything you know about her.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:17.010
Honestly, I've been
worried about her, too.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:22.600
I was glad to hear that
she's back to making manga,

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:28.690
but since it seems that she
doesn't like me, I'm not sure I can help.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:29.860
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:34.780
At one time, she and I
used to get along well.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:40.370
But then she suddenly acted cold
and we drifted apart.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:45.660
Perhaps I did something rude
to her without knowing.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:51.920
Honjo is a kind and friendly person,
but as for her life before an artist...

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:57.970
She rarely spoke about
the friends she had in the past.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:05.850
And I feel like she suddenly distances
herself from any friends in the making.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:09.980
If only I knew what I did to upset her,

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:14.070
I'd take that chance to apologize, but...

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:19.740
I bet Raziel played a part in this.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:26.250
If you had the power to know anything,
you'd look up those around you.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.620
True...

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:32.460
That probably made Nia
unable to trust other people.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:39.260
Everyone's said or done mean things
behind people's backs to some extent.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.970
You'd realize how
pathetic people are in no time.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:51.940
She only opens her heart to 2D
because she knows they won't betray her.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:52.980
That's--

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.820
--You think that's all it is?
--Huh?

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:59.360
Raziel shows her people's dark side.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:04.870
But knowing Nia's personality,
I feel like she'd look past that.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:09.120
Anyway, let's focus on the doujinshi.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:14.630
We need another chance to talk with Nia.
Without that, we'll get nowhere.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:32.440
Finally! Page 57 is done!

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:35.400
I just finished 58, too.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:43.160
I, whom only hurricanes can subdue,
have finished the last page!

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:42.860
"Don't worry about it. Besides, we'd have
been in trouble if you hadn't come."
"Hey, Natsumi."

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:49.040
Gather. I'll scan all our pages
and make it digital.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:54.040
With editing and printing,
it's gonna be a close one.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:57.750
Good work, Shido.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:02.840
You look exhausted, too.
What have you been up to?

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.600
It's a secret, Shido.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.220
Look forward to it.

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:11.770
Are you okay, Natsumi?

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:18.020
Natsumi, how about a break?

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.360
Oh, right.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:24.160
Swap out. You've been working non-stop.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:29.120
No, it's fine. I'm almost done.

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:34.040
You did the storyboard, draft,
and worked harder than anyone.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:39.960
That's right. The convention is
the real battle. Leave the rest to us.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:43.840
Agreed. You've worked
way too hard, Natsumi.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:46.300
Rest is important, too.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:51.060
It's okay. I won't be
that much use at the convention.

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:54.480
This is about all I can do, so...

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.060
But...

00:20:56.060 --> 00:21:01.650
You see, I'm really glad
I was saved by all of you guys.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:07.450
This time, I can do my part
to help another Spirit.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:11.540
That really... really makes me happy.

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:17.460
So, this is nothing.
I wanna show that dummy Nia, too:

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.920
That friends are a wonderful thing.

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:25.970
"H-Hey, Natsumi?"

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:29.600
And that's... the last... one.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.720
Natsumi?!

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:36.520
Good work, Natsumi.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:40.730
"Dummies..."
"*W-Waaah*"
"H-Hey, Natsumi?"

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:46.030
Now we have our weapon.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:49.990
Guys, we've gotta win, no matter what!

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:55.000
"Episode 02:
'So Be It! 2D It Is!'"

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:53.910
Now then, shall we begin our date?

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:29.550
The doujinshi convention
is a battle of passion!

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:34.600
The love and fervor of artists
heats up the winter cold!

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:37.850
Next time: "What's Yours Is Mine."

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:41.540
"Episode 03: 'What's Yours Is Mine.'"

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:41.490
Westcott's intentions are finally known.
